FROM (VALUES
  ('209542', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Mechanical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Electrical and Computer Engineering','Bioengineering','Business Administration','Business Analytics','Biology','Data Science','Psychology','Economics']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Mechanical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Electrical and Computer Engineering','Bioengineering','Biology','Data Science']::text[], '2026-27', 38190, 16386, 2592, 3, 6, 70, 100, 3.7, 1140, 1400, 'optional', '{"EA": "2026-11-02", "Winter": "2026-12-08", "Priority": "2027-02-01", "Spring": "2027-03-03"}', 'CDS 2025-26 C12 = 3.70. Min GPA 3.0 (NCAA scale) and English minimums (TOEFL iBT 70, IELTS 6.0, Duolingo 100) from international first-year degree page. Deadlines from general undergraduate (Corvallis) first-year deadlines page, not an international-specific table; Fall 2027 EA Nov 2 2026 and Priority Feb 1 2027, plus Winter 2027/Spring 2027 first-year terms. fees_usd = CDS 2025-26 G1 required fees first-year 2026-27. Health insurance = $2,880 for 3 terms (UG first-year column of international Program Prices page, estimated 2025-26 prices). Tuition and fees are combined on the price page, so fees come from the CDS. | health_insurance_usd=2880 | Sources: https://institutionalresearch.oregonstate.edu/sites/institutionalresearch.oregonstate.edu/files/2026-06/CDS-2025-26_1.pdf ; https://admissions.oregonstate.edu/international/programs/undergraduate-degree-programs/first-year-freshman ; https://admissions.oregonstate.edu/undergraduate-admission-deadlines ; https://admissions.oregonstate.edu/international/prices-scholarships/program-prices ; https://catalog.oregonstate.edu/programs/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?209542-Oregon-State-University', '2026-10-05'),
  ('207388', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science, BS','Mechanical Engineering, BSME','Aerospace Engineering, BSAE','Electrical Engineering, BSEE','Chemical Engineering, BSCH','Civil Engineering, BSCV','Biochemistry, BS','Biology, BS','Psychology, BS','Economics, BS','Hospitality and Tourism Management, BSBA','Chemistry, BS']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science, BS','Mechanical Engineering, BSME','Aerospace Engineering, BSAE','Electrical Engineering, BSEE','Chemical Engineering, BSCH','Civil Engineering, BSCV','Biochemistry, BS','Biology, BS','Chemistry, BS']::text[], '2026-27', 25754, 11230, 4008, 3, 5.5, 61, 95, 3.76, 1040, 1250, 'optional', '{"Fall": "2027-06-01", "Spring": "2026-11-01", "Priority": "2027-02-01"}', 'CDS 2025-26 C12 avg HS GPA 3.76 (99.63% reported). Min GPA 3.0 is for assured admission (recalculated by OSU). TOEFL iBT 61 from 2026-27 catalog; admissions page now lists only new-scale 3.5+. IELTS 5.5 / DET 95 are full-admission minimums (conditional admission available with TOEFL 48, IELTS 5.0, DET 85). SAT/ACT: CDS C8A ''not required for admission, but considered if submitted''. Deadlines (applicants outside the U.S.; in-U.S. dates are one month later): Fall June 1 (assumed Fall 2027), Spring Nov 1 2026, Priority = Feb 1 priority scholarship deadline; Nov 1 2026 early scholarship deadline also exists. fees_usd computed: $2,004 mandatory fees per semester x 2 (block rate 12-18 credits); excludes $150/semester international status fee and college fees. health_insurance_usd is the ''Health and Insurance'' estimate in the 2026-27 Financial Guarantee (estimate, not a plan premium). Majors from catalog A-Z index. | health_insurance_usd=2773 | Sources: https://ira.okstate.edu/site-files/documents/cds/CDS-2025-2026-PDF.pdf ; https://go.okstate.edu/admissions/international/freshman/requirements.html ; https://catalog.okstate.edu/about/admissions/international/ ; https://go.okstate.edu/admissions/international/dates-deadlines ; https://bursar.okstate.edu/tuition_fees/tuition_fees ; https://go.okstate.edu/admissions/international/files/docs/2026-2027-financial-guarantee.pdf ; https://catalog.okstate.edu/azindex/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?207388-Oklahoma-State-University-Main-Campus', '2026-10-05'),
  ('243780', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Data Science','Artificial Intelligence','Mechanical Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Computer Engineering','Aeronautical and Astronautical Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Industrial Engineering','Accounting']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Data Science','Artificial Intelligence','Mechanical Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Computer Engineering','Aeronautical and Astronautical Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Industrial Engineering']::text[], '2026-27', 28794, 12820, 274, NULL, 6.5, 88, 115, 3.81, 1200, 1480, 'required', '{"EA": "2026-11-01", "RD": "2027-01-15"}', 'avg_gpa4 = CDS 2025-26 C12 (3.81); CDS now covers West Lafayette + Indianapolis + Polytechnic Statewide combined. No min GPA stated. TOEFL 88 (min 20/section) for exams before 2026-01-21; new scale 4.5 (4.0/section). IELTS 6.5 (6.0 per section), Duolingo 115 (110 subscores). SAT/ACT: CDS C8A (Fall 2027 applicants) marks tests as required; admissions page says apply with an SAT, ACT or CLT score by Nov 1. Deadlines: EA Nov 1 (full consideration/scholarships); fall application window closes Jan 15; page gives month/day only, year inferred as 2026-27 cycle. Fees $274 = fitness/wellness 234 + student activity 40 (2026-27); international students additionally pay $3,310/yr International Student Tuition (not a fee here). Health insurance is mandatory for international students but premium is not published on official Purdue pages -> null. | Sources: https://www.purdue.edu/idata/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/CDS-2025-2026.xlsx ; https://admissions.purdue.edu/become-student/english-proficiency/ ; https://admissions.purdue.edu/become-student/apply/ ; https://www.purdue.edu/treasurer/finance/bursar-office/tuition/fee-rates-2026-2027/undergraduate-tuition-and-fees-2026-2027/ ; https://engineering.purdue.edu/Engr/Academics/Undergraduate/Majors', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?243780-Purdue-University-Main-Campus', '2026-10-05'),
  ('214777', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Software Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Computer Engineering','Civil Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Aerospace Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Cybersecurity Analytics and Operations','Data Sciences','Statistics']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Software Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Computer Engineering','Civil Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Aerospace Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Cybersecurity Analytics and Operations','Data Sciences','Statistics']::text[], '2026-27', 41790, 14474, 640, NULL, 6.5, 80, 120, 3.67, 1240, 1420, 'optional', '{"EA": "2026-11-01"}', 'University Park campus. avg_gpa4 3.67 = CDS 2025-26 C12 (96% submitted GPA); CDS 2024-25 reported 3.84. TOEFL 80 applies to exams before Jan 21 2026; new scale minimum 4.5. English can also be met via SAT EBRW 570, ACT English 24, etc. Penn State is test-optional. Early Action deadline Nov 1 (page gives no year; assumed Fall 2027 entry); no Regular Decision, rolling after Nov 1. Required fees $640 from CDS G1 (2026-27). SHIP $4,365 for undergraduates 2026-27 (F/J students must buy or waive). No minimum GPA stated for international applicants. | health_insurance_usd=4365 | Sources: https://opair.psu.edu/files/2026/06/UniversityPark_CDS_2025_2026.pdf ; https://www.psu.edu/resources/international-students/admission-requirements ; https://www.psu.edu/resources/international-students/deadlines ; https://www.psu.edu/news/student-affairs/story/rates-announced-2026-27-student-health-insurance-plan ; https://admissions.psu.edu/academics/majors/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?214777-Pennsylvania-State-University-Main-Campus', '2026-10-05'),
  ('123961', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Computer Engineering & Computer Science','Mechanical Engineering','Electrical & Computer Engineering','Aerospace Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Industrial & Systems Engineering','Business Administration','Economics','Neuroscience']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Computer Engineering & Computer Science','Mechanical Engineering','Electrical & Computer Engineering','Aerospace Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Industrial & Systems Engineering','Neuroscience']::text[], '2026-27', 72097, 19931, 1952, NULL, 7, 100, 130, 3.8, 1450, 1550, 'optional', '{"ED": "2026-11-01", "EA": "2026-11-01", "RD": "2027-01-10", "RD_performing_arts": "2026-12-01"}', 'avg_gpa4 = CDS 2024-25 C12 (3.80); 2025-26 CDS not found. No min GPA stated. TOEFL 100 (min 20 per section) for exams before 2026-01-21; new scale min 5 overall. IELTS 7. Duolingo 130 on the official international page (a USC admissions blog says 135; official page used). English exam required for all non-native speakers, no waivers. SAT/ACT optional for 2027-28 entry. Fees $1,952 = 2026-27 undergraduate budget; USC does not list health insurance in the aid budget and the premium was not readable on official pages, so health_insurance_usd is null. Majors from the USC transfer guide PDF (official). | Sources: https://oir.usc.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2025/10/CDS_2024-2025_FINAL-3.pdf ; https://admission.usc.edu/prospective-students/how-to-apply/international-students/ ; https://admission.usc.edu/apply/dates-deadlines/ ; https://financialaid.usc.edu/undergraduate-financial-aid/cost-of-attendance/ ; https://admission.usc.edu/wp-content/uploads/transferring-to-usc.pdf', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?123961-University-of-Southern-California', '2026-10-05'),
  ('171100', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Communication','Computer Science','Engineering','Biology','Psychology','Social Sciences','Business']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Engineering','Biology']::text[], '2026-27', 43842, 12564, 1840, NULL, 6.5, 79, 110, 3.74, 1180, 1360, 'optional', '{"EA": "2026-11-01", "Priority": "2027-02-01", "RD": "2027-04-01"}', 'avg_gpa4 from CDS 2025-26 C12 (3.74). Min scores are for regular (non-provisional) admission; TOEFL 79 is for tests before 1/21/26 (new scale: 4, no section below 4 except speaking 3.5). Provisional admission accepted at TOEFL 60-78, IELTS 6.0, DET 95-105. No minimum GPA/requirements stated (min_gpa4 null; middle 50% HS GPA 3.5-4.0). Deadline pages give no year; dates assigned to the fall 2027 cycle. fees_usd = (Undergraduate Student Fee $750 + Recreation & Wellness fee $170) x 2 semesters, Fall 2026/Spring 2027; excludes college program fees and student-voted taxes. No official 2026-27 undergraduate health insurance premium confirmed. Majors list is limited to those confirmed from search of official MSU pages; CS is restricted/moratorium status per Registrar. | Sources: https://edge.sitecorecloud.io/michiganstab57e-msustrategi129d-prod9868-7e5e/media/project/msu/ir/docs/cds/cds-2025-2026.pdf ; https://admissions.msu.edu/apply/international/language-requirements ; https://admissions.msu.edu/apply/international ; https://admissions.msu.edu/apply/international/admission-criteria ; https://admissions.msu.edu/apply/international/dates-and-deadlines ; https://controller.msu.edu/student-accounts/tuition-rates-by-semester/international-undergrad-fall-spring ; https://reg.msu.edu/academicprograms/ProgramDetail.aspx?Program=1328', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?171100-Michigan-State-University', '2026-10-05'),
  ('151351', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Informatics','Data Science','Intelligent Systems Engineering','Computer Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Robotics','Cybersecurity and Global Policy','Business Intelligence and Data Science']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Informatics','Data Science','Intelligent Systems Engineering','Computer Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Robotics','Cybersecurity and Global Policy','Business Intelligence and Data Science']::text[], '2026-27', 41891, 13984, 1522, NULL, 6.5, 79, 115, 3.8, 1170, 1400, 'optional', '{"EA": "2026-11-01", "RD": "2027-02-01"}', 'avg_gpa4 3.8 = CDS 2025-26 C12 (94.94% of first-years submitted GPA), 4.0 scale. Admissions class profile (2025 class) separately shows middle-50% admitted HS GPA 3.73-4.00. TOEFL 79 is iBT 0-120 scale; page lists these as admission standards (higher thresholds apply to begin classes: TOEFL 100 / IELTS 7.5). Deadlines: EA Nov 1, RD Feb 1; page gives month/day only, year inferred as 2026-27 cycle. fees_usd = CDS G1 required fees 2026-27. Health insurance not found. Majors only from Luddy School''s official list (other schools'' lists are dynamic and not readable). | Sources: https://iuapps.iu.edu/cds/ ; https://bloomington.iu.edu/admissions/apply/international/english-proficiency.html ; https://bloomington.iu.edu/admissions/apply/freshman/ ; https://bloomington.iu.edu/admissions/apply/international/deadlines.html ; https://luddy.iu.edu/academics/undergraduate/index.html', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?151351-Indiana-University-Bloomington', '2026-10-05'),
  ('211440', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Artificial Intelligence','Information Systems','Statistics & Data Science','Electrical and Computer Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Civil & Environmental Engineering','Mathematical Sciences','Physics','Economics']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Artificial Intelligence','Information Systems','Statistics & Data Science','Electrical and Computer Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Civil & Environmental Engineering','Mathematical Sciences','Physics']::text[], '2026-27', 66246, 18166, 1862, NULL, 7.5, 102, 135, 3.89, 1500, 1570, 'required', '{"ED": "2026-11-02", "RD": "2027-01-04"}', 'avg_gpa4 = CDS 2025-26 C12 (3.89, 99.7% reporting). No min GPA stated. TOEFL 102 is for exams before 2026-01-21 (new 1-6 scale: 5). Duolingo 135 overall. SAT/ACT: most colleges require a test (test-flexible: SAT/ACT/IB/AP etc.); College of Fine Arts is test-optional; Griffin School of Computer Science requires SAT/ACT. Deadline pages give month/day only (ED Nov 2, RD Jan 4; Drama and Music RD Dec 1; architecture/art/design Jan 5), year inferred as the 2026-27 cycle. Fees = first-year experience 748 + technology 490 + student activities 322 + transportation 302 (2026-27). Health insurance premium 2026-27 $3,093 (waivable). | health_insurance_usd=3093 | Sources: https://www.cmu.edu/ira/CDS/pdf/cds_2025_26/cds_2025_full_pdf.pdf ; https://www.cmu.edu/admission/admission/international-applicants ; https://www.cmu.edu/admission/admission/standardized-testing ; https://www.cmu.edu/admission/admission/application-plans-deadlines ; https://www.cmu.edu/sfs/tuition/undergraduate/index.html ; https://www.cmu.edu/admission/majors-programs', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?211440-Carnegie-Mellon-University', '2026-10-05'),
  ('153603', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Mechanical Engineering','Aerospace Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Data Science','Biology','Psychology','Kinesiology and Health','Animal Science','Finance','Architecture','Statistics']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Mechanical Engineering','Aerospace Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Data Science','Biology','Statistics']::text[], '2026-27', 28881, 10808, 1561, 3, 6, 71, 105, 3.76, 1120, 1360, 'optional', NULL, 'CDS 2025-26: C12 avg HS GPA 3.76; G1 required fees $1,561 (G1 heading in that CDS reads 2026-2027). Min GPA is ''equivalent to minimum 3.0 on 4.0 scale'' (waived by SAT 1200+/ACT 25+). TOEFL 71 (17+ Speaking/Writing) for tests before 2026-01-21; new scale 4.0 with min band 3.5 (per search excerpt). International admission is rolling: no fixed deadline dates, so deadlines null. No health insurance figure found. | Sources: https://www.ir.iastate.edu/files/documents/cds/CDS-25-26.pdf ; https://www.iastate.edu/admission-and-aid/admissions/international-admissions/international-first-year-requirements ; https://www.iastate.edu/admission-and-aid/admissions/international-admissions/english-proficiency-requirement ; https://www.iastate.edu/academics/majors-minors-certificates', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?153603-Iowa-State-University', '2026-10-05'),
  ('201645', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Aerospace Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Data Science and Analytics','Biology','Chemistry','Physics','Economics']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Aerospace Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Data Science and Analytics','Biology','Chemistry','Physics']::text[], '2026-27', 66608, 18762, 1390, NULL, 7, 90, 115, 3.78, 1430, 1540, 'optional', '{"EA": "2026-11-01", "ED": "2026-11-01", "ED2": "2027-01-15", "RD": "2027-01-15"}', 'avg_gpa4 3.78 = CDS 2025-26 C12 (CDS C11 instructs a 4.0 scale). First-year page says there is no minimum GPA or test score (min_gpa4 null). TOEFL 90 iBT (577 paper) for tests on or before Jan 20 2026; 4.5 on the new scale after. English waiver with SAT EBRW 630 or ACT English 26. fees_usd = Activity $530 + Matriculation $760 + RTA transport $100 (2026-27, Fall+Spring); health = Student Medical Plan $4,220 (subject to approval, waivable with comparable coverage). Deadlines: month/day on page, year inferred as upcoming cycle. | health_insurance_usd=4220 | Sources: https://case.edu/ir/sites/default/files/2026-02/CDS%202025-26%20Adjusted%20Final.pdf ; https://case.edu/admission/apply/international-applicants ; https://case.edu/admission/apply/first-year-applicants ; https://case.edu/admission/apply/deadlines-and-requirements ; https://case.edu/studentaccounts/tuition-fees/undergraduate-tuition-fees ; https://bulletin.case.edu/undergraduatestudies/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?201645-Case-Western-Reserve-University', '2026-10-05'),
  ('199193', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Mechanical Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Aerospace Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Business Administration','Economics','Biochemistry','Psychology','Statistics']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Mechanical Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Aerospace Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Biochemistry','Statistics']::text[], '2026-27', 32847, 14332, 2515.5, NULL, 6.5, 80, 110, 3.84, 1300, 1470, 'optional', '{"EA": "2026-11-01", "RD": "2027-01-15"}', 'CDS 2025-26 C12 avg HS GPA 3.84 (C11 says 4.0 scale; weighting not stated, so treat with caution). Min scores are for full admission: TOEFL iBT 80 (>=18 per section) for tests before Jan 21 2026, new 1-6 scale 4.5; IELTS 6.5 (6.0 per band); DET 110. SAT/ACT optional (page: optional for applicants at US schools with weighted GPA >= 2.8; CDS: test-optional). Spring entry deadline Oct 1 already passed. fees_usd = 2 x $1,257.75 required fees, nonresident (computed). health_insurance_usd = 2 x $1,312 Student Blue per semester (computed); admissions page estimates $2,703 for Fall 2027 entry. Majors from search excerpt of official catalog pages. | health_insurance_usd=2624 | Sources: https://report.isa.ncsu.edu/ir/cds/pdfs/CDS_2025-26.v1.pdf ; https://admissions.ncsu.edu/apply/international/first-year/ ; https://studentservices.ncsu.edu/finances/tuition-and-fees/tuition-and-fee-rates/undergraduate-students/ ; https://studentservices.ncsu.edu/finances/tuition-and-fees/health-insurance-requirement/ ; https://catalog.ncsu.edu/undergraduate/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?199193-North-Carolina-State-University-at-Raleigh', '2026-10-05'),
