  ('110653', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Computer Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Aerospace Engineering','Civil Engineering','Data Science','Software Engineering','Biological Sciences','Mathematics','Economics']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Computer Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Aerospace Engineering','Civil Engineering','Data Science','Software Engineering','Biological Sciences','Mathematics']::text[], '2025-26', 49922, 18991, 2880, 3.4, 6.5, 80, 115, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'not_accepted', '{"Fall": "2026-11-30"}', 'avg_gpa4 null: CDS 2025-26 C12 not populated (admissions page only gives admitted-class unweighted median 3.95 / weighted 4.19 for 2025, not an enrolled average). min_gpa4 3.4 = nonresident minimum in the 15 A-G courses (3.0 for CA residents). TOEFL iBT min 80 is the pre-Jan-2026 scale; new-scale min is 4.5. Deadline = UC Application submission period Oct 1 - Nov 30 (fall 2027). fees_usd = sum of mandatory fees for the 2025-26 undergrad cohort, excluding health insurance and nonresident supplemental tuition (SSF 1,332 + ASUCI 157.06 + Student Center 457.05 + Bren Events 69 + Rec Center 264 + Spirit 99 + Measure S 24 + TGIF 10.5 + Anteater Express 160.03 + Club Sports 21 + SOAR 26.63 + Food Pantry 12.28 + eTech 247.5 = 2,880.05); one-time document/writing placement fees excluded. health = USHIP 2,845.71 (waivable). A 2026-27 fee page exists (https://reg.uci.edu/fees/2026-2027/undergrad_26.html) but could not be read reliably. | health_insurance_usd=2846 | Sources: https://admissions.uci.edu/apply/first-year-students/index.php ; https://admissions.uci.edu/apply/international-students.php ; https://admissions.uci.edu/apply/index.php ; https://reg.uci.edu/fees/2025-2026/undergrad_25.html ; https://catalogue.uci.edu/undergraduatedegrees/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?110653-University-of-California-Irvine', '2026-10-05'),
  ('204796', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science and Engineering','Computer and Information Science','Mechanical Engineering','Aerospace Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Electrical and Computer Engineering','Industrial and Systems Engineering','Data Analytics','Finance','Economics']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science and Engineering','Computer and Information Science','Mechanical Engineering','Aerospace Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Electrical and Computer Engineering','Industrial and Systems Engineering','Data Analytics']::text[], '2026-27', 40022, 14738, NULL, NULL, 6.5, 79, 120, NULL, 1310, 1480, 'required', '{"EA": "2026-11-01", "RD": "2027-01-15"}', 'CDS 2025-26 and earlier PDFs have unreadable (non-extractable) values so avg_gpa4 null. TOEFL min 79 is for tests before 1/21/26; new 1-6 scale min is 4.0. Min scores can also be met by ACT English 21+ or SAT EBRW 550+. SAT/ACT stated as required for Columbus first-year applicants on the international freshmen page. Deadlines: Autumn 2027 EA Nov 1 2026, RD Jan 15 2027; Spring 2027 Oct 1 2026. 2026-27 non-resident costs: tuition and fees $14,034 + non-resident fees $30,220; mandatory fees not itemized; annual International Undergraduate Student Fee $3,103; health insurance estimate $4,108. fees_usd null (not itemized). | health_insurance_usd=4108 | Sources: https://undergrad.osu.edu/apply/international-freshmen/apply-step-by-step ; https://undergrad.osu.edu/cost-and-aid/basic-costs ; https://undergrad.osu.edu/majors-and-academics/majors-by-college', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?204796-Ohio-State-University-Main-Campus', '2026-10-05'),
  ('170976', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Mechanical Engineering','Data Science','Biology','Biomedical Engineering','Biomolecular Science','Microbiology','Molecular, Cellular, and Developmental Biology','Biology, Health, and Society']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Mechanical Engineering','Data Science','Biology','Biomedical Engineering','Biomolecular Science','Microbiology','Molecular, Cellular, and Developmental Biology']::text[], '2026-27', 60946, 15328, NULL, NULL, 7, 100, NULL, 3.9, 1360, 1530, 'optional', '{"ED": "2026-11-01", "EA": "2026-11-01", "RD": "2027-02-01"}', 'Avg GPA 3.9 (4.0 scale, unweighted) from CDS 2025-26 C12, 97.8% of first-years reported GPA. English: TOEFL iBT 100 range (sections 23+ reading/listening, 21+ speaking/writing; new 1-6 TOEFL: 5-6 range), IELTS 7.0 range (sections 6.5+); these are ''acceptable ranges'', not hard cutoffs. Duolingo English Test is NOT accepted for first-year admission, so min_duolingo is null. admissions.umich.edu pages returned HTTP 403 to direct fetch, so English scores, deadlines and test-optional status come from official-domain search result text, not a page read. fees_usd = CDS 2025-26 G1 (2026-27 year): required fees $494 for all students plus $1,000 extra required fee for international students; the CDS PDF text lost field alignment so this mapping is likely but not certain. Health insurance: U-M International Student plan is mandatory for F-1 students (waivable only for comparable US coverage) but the premium was not confirmed, so null. Majors list from official-domain search text (LSA and Engineering). | fees_usd omitted: CDS text unclear | Sources: https://obp.umich.edu/wp-content/uploads/pubdata/cds/cds_2025-26_umaa.pdf ; https://admissions.umich.edu/apply/international-applicants/exams-visas ; https://admissions.umich.edu/apply/first-year-applicants/requirements-deadlines ; https://admissions.umich.edu/academics-majors/majors-degrees', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?170976-University-of-Michigan-Ann-Arbor', '2026-10-05'),
  ('228778', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Mechanical Engineering','Aerospace Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Electrical and Computer Engineering','Petroleum Engineering','Business Administration (BBA)','Biology','Biochemistry','Mathematics']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Mechanical Engineering','Aerospace Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Electrical and Computer Engineering','Petroleum Engineering','Biology','Biochemistry','Mathematics']::text[], '2026-27', 44908, 14828, NULL, NULL, 6.5, 79, 115, NULL, 1250, 1510, 'required', '{"EA": "2026-10-15", "RD": "2026-12-01"}', 'UT CDS PDFs are hosted on Box and could not be read, so avg_gpa4 null. TOEFL 79 is the 120-scale minimum (new 6-point scale: 4). SAT or ACT (or CLT) required for the 2026-27 cycle. Deadlines for fall 2027 entry: EA Oct 15 2026, RD Dec 1 2026; spring entry Sept 1 (year assumed 2026 for spring 2027). Nonresident tuition range 2026-27 is $42,554-$51,106 and already includes mandatory fees (not itemized), so fees_usd null; ISSS support services fee ($125/semester) came only from a search summary, not confirmed. health_insurance_usd = UT SHIP fall $1,297.80 + spring $1,622.25 = $2,920.05 incl. 5% admin fee (2026-27). Majors list assembled from search of official UT catalog pages. | health_insurance_usd=2920.05 | Sources: https://admissions.utexas.edu/info-for/international-students/ ; https://admissions.utexas.edu/apply/freshman/ ; https://global.utexas.edu/isss/advising-services/insurance/costs ; https://onestop.utexas.edu/managing-costs/cost-tuition-rates/cost-of-attendance/ ; https://catalog.utexas.edu/undergraduate/degree-programs/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?228778-The-University-of-Texas-at-Austin', '2026-10-05'),
  ('104179', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Mechanical Engineering','Aerospace Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Electrical and Computer Engineering','Civil Engineering','Software Engineering','Systems Engineering','Mining Engineering','Optical Sciences & Engineering','Industrial Engineering','Chemical Engineering']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Mechanical Engineering','Aerospace Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Electrical and Computer Engineering','Civil Engineering','Software Engineering','Systems Engineering','Mining Engineering','Optical Sciences & Engineering','Industrial Engineering','Chemical Engineering']::text[], '2026-27', 42278, 16746, NULL, NULL, 6.5, 79, 110, NULL, 1150, 1420, 'optional', '{"EA": "2026-11-01"}', 'avg_gpa4 null: CDS 2025-26 PDF (uair.arizona.edu/sites/default/files/2026-06/CDS_PDF_2025-26_v02_RE-PRINT.pdf) has empty C12 values. No minimum GPA found for international first-years. English minimums are the ''Admissions Minimum'' table; TOEFL 79 is for tests before Jan 2026, new 1-6 scale minimum is 4 (min_toefl uses old scale). Fall 2027 Early Action Nov 1 2026; later applications move to Regular Decision (no date given). Fees null: non-resident undergraduate mandatory fee line in Bursar chart is illegible/blank; international student fee is $200 per semester for F-1/J-1 (https://international.arizona.edu/international-students/cost-attendance). Health insurance mandatory via UA Student Health Insurance Plan but no amount published on pages read. Majors are College of Engineering list only (the campus-wide degree search is dynamic and was not readable). | Sources: https://www.arizona.edu/admissions/undergraduate/international ; https://www.arizona.edu/admissions/undergraduate/first-year ; https://www.arizona.edu/admissions/deadlines ; https://engineering.arizona.edu/undergrad/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?104179-University-of-Arizona', '2026-10-05'),
  ('230764', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Mechanical Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Computer Engineering','Biology','Economics','Psychology','Finance','Nursing','Mathematics']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Mechanical Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Computer Engineering','Biology','Mathematics']::text[], '2026-27', 30860, 13315, NULL, NULL, 6.5, 80, 110, NULL, 1190, 1380, 'optional', '{"Spring": "2026-11-15", "EA": "2026-12-01"}', 'avg_gpa4 3.64 = CDS 2025-26 C12 (98% submitted), read from a search excerpt of the official PDF; the PDF itself returned 404 when fetched directly. No minimum GPA (admissions-standards page: ''no minimum GPA to be admitted''). TOEFL 80/120 (4.5/6 alt), IELTS 6.5, Duolingo 110 from English Proficiency page. Deadlines: freshman page shows Spring Nov 15, Early Action & Merit Dec 1, Fall Apr 1 / Summer Apr 1 (month/day only, next cycle assumed); the international freshman page instead lists Spring Nov 15, Summer May 1, Fall Aug 1 - conflicting Fall date so Fall omitted. fees_usd null: Utah publishes tuition and fees combined ($32,932 on 2026-27 I-20 estimate; plus $300 international student fee and $75 one-time orientation fee). Health insurance $3,000 is the I-20 budget estimate for 2026-27. | health_insurance_usd=3000 | some low-confidence values omitted | Sources: https://data.utah.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/CDS_2025-2026.pdf ; https://admissions.utah.edu/apply/international/english-proficiency/ ; https://admissions.utah.edu/apply/freshman-students/ ; https://admissions.utah.edu/apply/international/international-freshman-admissions-undergraduate-costs/ ; https://majormaps.utah.edu/majors_list/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?230764-University-of-Utah', '2026-10-05'),
  ('122755', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Communication','Engineering','Psychology','Social Sciences','Visual & Performing Arts','Health Professions','Business']::text[], ARRAY['Engineering']::text[], '2026-27', 21010, 20971, NULL, 3, 6, 61, 95, 3.5, NULL, NULL, 'not_accepted', '{"Fall": "2027-04-01"}', 'Avg GPA 3.50 from CDS 2025-26 C12 (99.41% submitted GPA). English minimums are for most majors: TOEFL iBT 61 (new 1-6 scale: 3.5), IELTS 6.0, DET 95; Engineering majors need TOEFL 80 (new scale 4.0) and IELTS 6.5, DET 95. min_gpa4 3.00 is the a-g GPA minimum for international freshmen (from official-domain search text; some majors and impacted programs require higher). CSU/SJSU does not consider SAT/ACT for fall 2027 admission (scores only for placement after admission). International fall 2027 deadline April 1 2027 (Cal State Apply opens Aug 1, submit from Oct 1 2026); SJSU is impacted. Cost table gives only a combined undergraduate ''Tuition & Fees'' $20,538 (2026-27, 12 units/semester, includes $420/unit nonresident tuition), no separate mandatory-fee line, so fees_usd is null. Health insurance estimate $2,250/yr (mandatory for F-1). Majors list is partial: only Computer Science and Software Engineering were confirmed from official-domain results. | health_insurance_usd=2250 | Sources: https://www.sjsu.edu/irsa/docs/cds/20260113_CDS%202025%20FINAL.pdf ; https://www.sjsu.edu/global/about/international-students/applying-to-sjsu/ ; https://www.sjsu.edu/admissions/international-freshman/admission-requirements/english-proficiency.php ; https://www.sjsu.edu/admissions/impaction/index.php ; https://www.sjsu.edu/admissions/deadlines/index.php ; https://www.sjsu.edu/admissions/internationalfinancialdocs.php', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?122755-San-Jose-State-University', '2026-10-05'),
  ('134130', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Computer Engineering','Data Science','Electrical Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Aerospace Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Physics','Psychology','Economics']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Computer Engineering','Data Science','Electrical Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Aerospace Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Physics']::text[], '2026-27', 28659, 12120, 3070, 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3.9, 1320, 1480, 'required', '{"ED": "2026-10-15", "EA": "2026-11-01", "RD": "2027-01-15"}', 'avg_gpa4 3.9 = CDS 2025-26 C12 (Fall 2025 entrants). min_gpa4 2.0 is the stated minimum cumulative GPA for freshman applicants (admission is far more competitive). UF''s freshman admissions pages and catalog say non-native speakers must submit TOEFL or IELTS but state no freshman minimum scores (the 80 / 6.0 figures appear only on UF Online and transfer pages), so min_ielts/min_toefl/min_duolingo are null; Duolingo acceptance for freshmen not confirmed. Deadlines are the 2026-27 cycle (ED Oct 15, EA Nov 1, RD Jan 15). fees_usd 3070 = required fees for nonresidents in CDS G1 for 2026-27 (stated as tuition & fees $30,886 minus tuition $27,816). Health insurance $3,185 is the International Center''s mandatory undergraduate estimate (2026-27); UHCSR plan opt-out/waiver is limited for international students. | health_insurance_usd=3185 | Sources: https://data-apps.ir.aa.ufl.edu/public/cds/CDS%202025-26_v7_07.15.2026.pdf ; https://admissions.ufl.edu/apply/freshman/requirements ; https://admissions.ufl.edu/apply/freshman/deadlines ; https://internationalcenter.ufl.edu/iss/obtaining-f-1-status/start-up-cost/ ; https://catalog.ufl.edu/UGRD/programs/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?134130-University-of-Florida', '2026-10-05'),
  ('110671', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Computer Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Bioengineering','Chemical Engineering','Data Science','Biology','Biochemistry','Mathematics','Statistics','Business Administration']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Computer Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Bioengineering','Chemical Engineering','Data Science','Biology','Biochemistry','Mathematics','Statistics']::text[], '2026-27', 49806, 20691, NULL, 3.4, 6.5, 80, 115, 3.75, NULL, NULL, 'not_accepted', '{"RD": "2026-11-30"}', 'CDS 2025-26 C12 = 3.75. TOEFL 80 is for tests before Jan 2026; page states 4.5 on the new scale from Jan 2026. Min GPA 3.4 is the first-year GPA stated on the international page. SAT/ACT not considered. Deadline: UC application fall filing period is Nov 1-30 (assumed Fall 2027 cycle, recorded as 2026-11-30). fees_usd null: CDS 2025-26 G1 required fees blank/''varies according to cohort year''. Health insurance not found. | Sources: https://ir.ucr.edu/sites/default/files/2026-05/cds-2025-2026.pdf ; https://admissions.ucr.edu/international ; https://admissions.ucr.edu/majors', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?110671-University-of-California-Riverside', '2026-10-05'),
  ('126614', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Aerospace Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Electrical and Computer Engineering','Business Administration','Economics','Psychology','Integrative Physiology','Environmental Studies','Journalism','Information Science','Neuroscience']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Aerospace Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Electrical and Computer Engineering','Integrative Physiology','Neuroscience']::text[], '2026-27', 44918, 18468, NULL, NULL, 6.5, 80, 115, NULL, 1240, 1430, 'optional', '{"EA": "2026-11-15", "RD": "2027-01-15"}', 'TOEFL 80 is for pre-Jan-2026 tests (new 1-6 scale min 4.0). EA/RD are fall 2027 entry; spring deadline Oct 1 already passed. avg_gpa4 null: CDS is behind a SharePoint link, not readable. fees_usd null: many fees now bundled into tuition; separate fees (new student fee $500 intl, immigration compliance $40/sem) not summed. health_insurance_usd = 2 x $2,648 (Anthem Gold SHIP, computed; rates ''pending DOI approval''). Majors from search excerpt of official majors/catalog pages. No minimum GPA stated on first-year page. | health_insurance_usd=5296 | Sources: https://www.colorado.edu/admissions/process/international/plan/english-proficiency ; https://www.colorado.edu/admissions/process/first-year/apply ; https://www.colorado.edu/health/cu-gold-ship ; https://www.colorado.edu/academics/programs/majors', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?126614-University-of-Colorado-Boulder', '2026-10-05'),
  ('131469', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Biomedical Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Data Science','Biology','Finance','Accountancy','International Affairs','Political Science','Economics','Psychology','Statistics']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Biomedical Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Data Science','Biology','Statistics']::text[], '2026-27', 67710, 16920, 770, NULL, 6.5, 90, 120, NULL, 1350, 1500, NULL, '{"ED": "2026-11-01", "ED2": "2027-01-05", "RD": "2027-01-05"}', 'Admissions website returned 403, so test scores/deadlines come from the GW International Brochure 2025 (TOEFL 90 old scale; search excerpt of live page also lists 4.5 on new scale). Brochure dates are month/day (ED I Nov 1, ED II Jan 5, RD Jan 5); assumed next cycle (Fall 2027). CDS 2025-26 C12 average GPA left blank by GW so avg_gpa4 null. fees_usd = CDS G1 required fees first-year $770 (2026-27 heading). Health insurance $2,841 is from the brochure 2025-26 cost estimate. SAT policy not confirmed, null. | health_insurance_usd=2841 | Sources: https://undergraduate.admissions.gwu.edu/sites/g/files/zaxdzs4676/files/2025-08/International%20Brochure%202025.pdf ; https://irp.gwu.edu/sites/g/files/zaxdzs6056/files/2026-04/CDS-PDF-2025-2026.pdf', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?131469-George-Washington-University', '2026-10-05'),
  ('122597', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Biology','Business Administration','Computer Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Psychology','Kinesiology','Nursing','Cinema','Economics']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Biology','Computer Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Chemistry','Biochemistry','Applied Mathematics']::text[], '2026-27', 20550, 22266, 1982, 2.5, 6, 61, 95, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'not_accepted', '{"Priority": "2026-11-30", "Fall": "2027-05-01"}', 'avg_gpa4 is from CDS 2020-21 C12 (3.31), the newest Common Data Set SF State posts at ir.sfsu.edu (file hosted on the IR site''s pantheonsite domain) - stale. Min GPA 2.5 (4.0 scale) for freshmen from high schools outside the US. English minimums: TOEFL iBT 61, IELTS 6.0, DET 95 (also PTE 45, SAT EBRW 550). CSU no longer uses ACT/SAT in admission determination, so sat_policy=not_accepted (scores only usable as English proof). Deadlines: Fall 2027 International Application Deadline May 1, 2027; Priority deadline for impacted majors Nov 30, 2026; Spring 2027 application closed Sep 30, 2026. fees_usd computed: mandatory local campus fees $991 per semester (Fall 2026 page subtotal $993 incl. optional $2 SIRF) x 2 for 6.1+ units; excludes tuition and nonresident tuition $471/unit. No F-1 undergraduate health insurance premium found (only a J-1 exchange plan page), so health_insurance_usd null. | some low-confidence values omitted | Sources: https://dev-sfsu-ir.pantheonsite.io/sites/default/files/documents/CDS_2020-2021_SFSU_0.pdf ; https://future.sfsu.edu/node/18 ; https://future.sfsu.edu/admissions/dates-deadlines ; https://bursar.sfsu.edu/students/upcoming-academic-year ; https://bulletin.sfsu.edu/programs/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?122597-San-Francisco-State-University', '2026-10-05'),
  ('228723', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Computer Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Aerospace Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Industrial Engineering','Economics','Mathematics','Biology']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Computer Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Aerospace Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Industrial Engineering','Mathematics','Biology']::text[], '2026-27', 40124, 13008, 3970, NULL, 6, 80, NULL, NULL, 1150, 1400, 'optional', '{"Spring": "2026-10-15", "Fall": "2026-12-01"}', 'TOEFL iBT 80 (tests before Jan 21 2026) or 4.5 overall with 4.0 per section (new scale); IELTS Academic 6.0; also accepts TOEFL Essentials 8.5, SAT EBRW 560, ACT English 21. Duolingo is not listed as accepted (null). CDS 2025-26 C12 average GPA is N/A so avg_gpa4 null. Deadlines: Spring Oct 15 and Fall Dec 1 are month/day on page, year inferred as upcoming cycle. fees_usd = first-year Required Fees from CDS 2025-26 G1 (labelled 2026-27). Health insurance cost not found. | Sources: https://admissions.tamu.edu/apply/international/international-freshman.html ; https://abpa.tamu.edu/accountability-rankings/common-data-set.html ; https://catalog.tamu.edu/undergraduate/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?228723-Texas-A-M-University-College-Station', '2026-10-05'),
  ('134097', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science (BS/BA)','Computational Biology (BS)','Cyber Criminology (BS)','Computer Programming and Applications (BA)','Dance','Film (Animation and Production)','Music','Theatre']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science (BS/BA)','Computational Biology (BS)','Cyber Criminology (BS)','Computer Programming and Applications (BA)']::text[], '2026-27', 18786, 13474, NULL, NULL, 6.5, 80, 125, NULL, 1270, 1410, 'required', '{"RD": "2026-12-01", "Rolling": "2027-03-01"}', 'TOEFL 80 applies to tests before 2026-01-21 (new 1-6 scale: 4.0). Duolingo 125 per admissions page (Undergraduate Bulletin search excerpt says 120). Deadlines: Early Decision is domestic only and Early Action is Florida residents only; RD Dec 1 and Rolling Mar 1 are open to international; page gives month/day only, assumed Fall 2027 cycle. SAT/ACT required by Florida BOG regulation 6.002. fees_usd = ''Fees'' line ($50) in FSU out-of-state 2026-27 cost estimate (flat, no breakdown; may not capture all mandatory fees). avg_gpa4 null: FSU CDS C12 not retrieved (CDS year links not reachable; FSU-reported HS GPAs are above 4.0 i.e. weighted). No health insurance figure on cost page. Majors list is partial (FSU Academic Program Guide not readable). | some low-confidence values omitted | Sources: https://admissions.fsu.edu/international/english-proficiency ; https://admissions.fsu.edu/international/first-year ; https://admissions.fsu.edu/first-year/apply ; https://tuition.fsu.edu/cost-attendance/cost-estimates-fall-2026-spring-2027 ; https://www.cs.fsu.edu/academics/undergraduate-programs/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?134097-Florida-State-University', '2026-10-05'),
  ('126818', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Mechanical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Chemical and Biological Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Computer Engineering','Construction Engineering','Environmental Engineering','Data Science']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Mechanical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Chemical and Biological Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Computer Engineering','Construction Engineering','Environmental Engineering','Data Science']::text[], '2026-27', 34783, 16817, 3243, NULL, 6, 72, 110, 3.7, NULL, NULL, 'optional', '{"Spring": "2026-11-01", "EA": "2026-12-01", "RD": "2027-02-01"}', 'CDS FY2026 (2025-26) C12 avg HS GPA 3.7. Direct-admission minimums: TOEFL iBT 72 (before Jan 2026; new scale 4.0), IELTS 6.0, Duolingo 110 (some other CSU pages list 80/6.5/120; the international-admissions page was used). No minimum GPA stated (3.0+ typical, not a minimum). Test-optional / SAT-ACT not required (search excerpt of CSU admissions). Deadlines: Fall EA Dec 1, RD Feb 1, Spring Nov 1 (month/day only; next cycle assumed). fees_usd = estimated mandatory fees for 15 credits; health insurance 2026-27. Majors from search excerpt of CSU engineering/CS catalog pages. | health_insurance_usd=2556 | Sources: https://www.ir.colostate.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/21/2026/03/CSU_CDS_FY2026_Access.pdf ; https://international.colostate.edu/iec/international-admissions/english-language-proficiency/ ; https://admissions.colostate.edu/apply/freshmen/ ; https://international.colostate.edu/iec/international-admissions/undergraduate-info/ ; https://international.colostate.edu/isss/resources/finances/estimated-expenses/ ; https://catalog.colostate.edu/general-catalog/programsaz/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?126818-Colorado-State-University-Fort-Collins', '2026-10-05'),
