  ('165015', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Biochemistry','Biology','Business','Chemistry','Computer Science','Economics','Mathematics','Neuroscience','Physics','Politics','Psychology','Quantitative Economics']::text[], ARRAY['Biochemistry','Biology','Chemistry','Computer Science','Mathematics','Neuroscience','Physics','Applied Mathematics']::text[], '2026-27', 68080, 19944, 598, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3.84, 1390, 1520, 'optional', '{"ED": "2026-11-02", "EA": "2026-11-02", "ED2": "2027-01-15", "RD": "2027-01-15", "Spring": "2026-11-02"}', 'avg_gpa4 = CDS 2025-26 C12 (3.84). No minimum TOEFL/IELTS/Duolingo published for undergraduates (English exam submitted by non-native speakers; exempt after 4+ yrs English-medium school). Test-optional policy. Deadlines from the dates page (Nov. 2 / Jan. 15, assumed fall 2027 cycle; Spring admission Nov. 2 for Jan 2027). fees_usd $598 = mandatory Student Activity Fee (CDS G1 2026-27, text layout scrambled); excludes international student fee ($252/semester) and new student fee. health_insurance_usd $4,700 = projected 2026-27 School Health Plan (from search excerpt of admissions affordability page; auto-enrolled, waivable). | health_insurance_usd=4700 | Sources: https://www.brandeis.edu/institutional-research/docs/cds-2025-26.pdf ; https://www.brandeis.edu/admissions/apply/international.html ; https://www.brandeis.edu/admissions/apply/dates.html ; https://www.brandeis.edu/admissions/affordability/tuition.html ; https://www.brandeis.edu/admissions/academics/majors-minors.html', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?165015-Brandeis-University', '2026-10-05'),
  ('196079', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Mechanical Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Industrial and Systems Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Accounting','Business Administration','Economics','Psychology','Chemistry','Physics','Nursing']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Mechanical Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Industrial and Systems Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Chemistry','Physics']::text[], '2026-27', 30447, 18809, 3497, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3.88, 1340, 1500, 'optional', '{"EA": "2026-11-01", "RD": "2027-03-15"}', 'CDS linked from the OIR page https://www.binghamton.edu/offices/oir/institutional-data/common-data-set.html (file header says 2024-2025 but content is Fall 2025 entering class and 2026-27 costs, i.e. the 2025-26 CDS): C12 = 3.88, required fees $3,497 (G1, 2026-27). No stated minimum GPA or English minimums: page gives only mid-50% ranges (TOEFL 80-95 old scale / 4.0-5.0 new, IELTS 6.5-7.0, Duolingo 110-120), so left null. International first-year deadlines: EA Nov 1 (priority), RD Mar 15 (priority); the general first-year page lists Jan 15 for regular, so confirm which applies. Dates are month/day, assumed Fall 2027 cycle. Health insurance = SUNY international plan annual rate 8/15/2026-8/14/2027 as read on the page ($2,371.21; a search snippet showed $2,403.01 so the page may have been updated). | health_insurance_usd=2371.21 | Sources: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Dcby2MF3MGue7PRpH2nOCbSCtwmgPPUG/view?usp=sharing ; https://www.binghamton.edu/admissions/undergraduate/apply/international/first-year.html ; https://www.binghamton.edu/international/student-scholar-services/health-insurance/rates-2018.html ; https://www.binghamton.edu/academics/programs/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?196079-Binghamton-University', '2026-10-05'),
