  ('234076', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Commerce','Economics','Nursing','Biology','Psychology','Mechanical Engineering','Systems Engineering','Data Science','Statistics','Neuroscience']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Biology','Mechanical Engineering','Systems Engineering','Data Science','Statistics','Neuroscience']::text[], '2026-27', 59512, 14800, 3793, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1410, 1540, 'optional', '{"ED": "2026-11-01", "EA": "2026-11-01", "RD": "2027-01-05"}', 'avg_gpa4 null: C12 average blank in CDS 2024-25 PDF (value shown is 81.47% submitting GPA); CDS 2025-26 is only an embedded Qlik app, not fetchable. No minimum GPA or minimum IELTS/TOEFL/Duolingo stated: English test strongly encouraged for non-native speakers, no cutoffs (https://admission.virginia.edu/i-am/international). SAT/ACT: test-optional for Fall 2027. Dates are month/day on page; assumed Fall 2027 cycle. fees_usd = required fees first-year $3,793 from CDS 2024-25 G1 (covers 2025-26; 2026-27 CDS not readable). Health insurance = UVA Student Health Plan annual student rate 2026-2027 $4,220 (may be waived with comparable coverage). | health_insurance_usd=4220 | Sources: https://admission.virginia.edu/admission/deadlines-instructions ; https://ira.virginia.edu/sites/g/files/jsddwu1106/files/2025-03/CDS_2024-2025_508.pdf ; https://studenthealth.virginia.edu/about/insurance/student-health-plan ; https://www.virginia.edu/academics/majors', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?234076-University-of-Virginia-Main-Campus', '2026-10-05'),
  ('130794', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Mechanical Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Applied Mathematics','Economics','Statistics and Data Science','Physics','Neuroscience','Political Science','Psychology']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Mechanical Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Chemical Engineering','Applied Mathematics','Statistics and Data Science','Physics','Neuroscience']::text[], '2026-27', 67250, 19900, 185, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1470, 1570, 'required', '{"EA": "2026-11-01", "RD": "2027-01-02"}', 'CDS 2025-26 and 2024-25 PDFs have C12 average GPA blank, so avg_gpa4 null. No official English minimums: standardized-testing page gives only ''most competitive'' benchmarks (TOEFL iBT >=100 old scale or 5 new scale, IELTS 7, DET 120), so min_* null. Deadline page lists month/day only (EA = Single-Choice Early Action Nov 1; RD Jan 2); year inferred as the 2026-27 cycle. fees_usd = Student Activity Fee 2026-27; health = Yale Health hospitalization and specialty coverage annual single-student rate 2026-27 (waivable). | health_insurance_usd=3764 | Sources: https://admissions.yale.edu/standardized-testing ; https://admissions.yale.edu/application-deadlines ; https://finaid.yale.edu/coa ; https://yalehealth.yale.edu/topic/student-rates-2026-2027 ; https://catalog.yale.edu/ycps/majors-in-yale-college/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?130794-Yale-University', '2026-10-05'),
  ('186131', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering','Operations Research and Financial Engineering','Electrical and Computer Engineering','Civil and Environmental Engineering','Chemical and Biological Engineering','Economics','Mathematics','Physics','Neuroscience','Molecular Biology','Politics']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering','Operations Research and Financial Engineering','Electrical and Computer Engineering','Civil and Environmental Engineering','Chemical and Biological Engineering','Mathematics','Physics','Neuroscience','Molecular Biology']::text[], '2026-27', 62688, 20250, 314, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1510, 1580, 'optional', '{"REA": "2026-11-01", "RD": "2027-01-01"}', 'No minimum TOEFL/IELTS/Duolingo stated on undergraduate pages (tests TOEFL, IELTS Academic, DET or PTE accepted; 3 years of English-medium secondary school exempts); the 100/7.0 figures found belong to a graduate school, not used. Avg GPA 3.95 is from CDS 2024-25 section C12 (PDF text extraction placed the value without its field label; 99.3% submitted GPA); CDS 2025-26 was not readable. Deadline pages give month/day only (Nov 1 single-choice early action, Jan 1 regular decision); years inferred for the fall 2027 entry cycle. Test-optional for fall 2026 and 2027 entry, required again for fall 2028 entry. Fees = mandatory fees $314 for first-years/sophomores ($670 seniors); health = Student Health Plan $4,220 for 2026-27 ($3,800 for 2025-26), required unless covered by a comparable plan. Majors are Princeton ''concentrations''; list is a subset taken from the official engineering and A.B. lists. | health_insurance_usd=4220 | avg_gpa4 omitted: CDS field mapping unverified | Sources: https://ir.princeton.edu/sites/g/files/toruqf2041/files/documents/CDS_2425_Princeton_v1.2.pdf ; https://admission.princeton.edu/apply/application-checklist ; https://admission.princeton.edu/apply/first-year-application-dates-deadlines ; https://finaid.princeton.edu/how-aid-works/student-budget ; https://odoc.princeton.edu/curriculum/concentrations', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?186131-Princeton-University', '2026-10-05'),
