  ('216287', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Engineering','Biology','Chemistry','Mathematics','Physics','Astronomy','Neuroscience','Economics','Psychology','Political Science','Linguistics']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Engineering','Biology','Chemistry','Mathematics','Physics','Astronomy','Neuroscience']::text[], '2026-27', 65494, 20308, 482, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1490, 1560, 'optional', '{"ED": "2026-11-15", "ED2": "2027-01-04", "RD": "2027-01-04"}', 'CDS 2025-26 C12 average GPA left blank -> null. English proficiency (TOEFL, IELTS or Duolingo) or video response is required for applicants schooled outside the US, but no minimum scores are published -> null. Test scores optional. Deadlines per 2026-27 cycle: ED Nov 15, ED II Jan 4, RD Jan 4. fees_usd = Student Activities Fee $482 for 2026-27 (CDS 2025-26 required fees $460). Health insurance cost ''varies'' on the cost page (SHIP available) -> null. | Sources: https://www.swarthmore.edu/admissions-aid/application-materials-deadlines ; https://www.swarthmore.edu/financial-aid/tuition-books-housing-food-plan-activities-fee ; https://www.swarthmore.edu/academics', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?216287-Swarthmore-College', '2026-10-05'),
  ('168342', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Economics','Biology','Chemistry','Physics','Mathematics','Statistics','Astrophysics','Psychology','Political Economy','Environmental Studies','Geosciences']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Biology','Chemistry','Physics','Mathematics','Statistics','Astrophysics','Environmental Studies','Geosciences']::text[], '2026-27', 68560, 17260, 340, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1490, 1570, 'optional', '{"ED": "2026-11-15", "RD": "2027-01-04"}', 'williams.edu and hub.williams.edu returned HTTP 403 to fetch, so ALL values come from search-result excerpts of official Williams pages (not opened directly). English proficiency: no exam required, TOEFL/IELTS/Duolingo welcome; competitive TOEFL 5-6 (new scale) is not a minimum, so min_* null. CDS 2025-26 PDF not readable (403), avg_gpa4 null. Deadlines ED Nov 15, RD Jan 4 (month/day only; next cycle assumed). Test-optional per first-year page (no end date stated). fees_usd = ''Activities and Residential House Fees'' $340 on 2026-27 comprehensive fee; health insurance $3,365 (auto-enrolled unless waived). Majors from search excerpt of 2026-27 catalog. | health_insurance_usd=3365 | Sources: https://www.williams.edu/admission-aid/how-to-apply/first-year/ ; https://www.williams.edu/admission-aid/apply/international/ ; https://catalog.williams.edu/tuition-fees/ ; https://catalog.williams.edu/2627/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?168342-Williams-College', '2026-10-05'),
  ('161004', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Economics','Biology','Biochemistry','Chemistry','Mathematics','Physics','Neuroscience','Psychology','Government and Legal Studies','History','Environmental Studies']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Biology','Biochemistry','Chemistry','Mathematics','Physics','Neuroscience']::text[], '2026-27', 67832, 18488, 700, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1470, 1550, 'optional', '{"ED": "2026-11-15", "ED2": "2027-01-05", "RD": "2027-01-05"}', 'Bowdoin has no minimum GPA or English-proficiency score (EPT optional; international page: does not have a minimum qualifying EPT score) so min_* are null. CDS 2025-26 (bowdoin.edu/ir/pdf/bowdoin-cds_2025-2026.pdf) C12 GPA field is blank (avg_gpa4 null). Test-optional for 50+ years. Deadlines: ED I Nov 15, ED II and RD Jan 5 (month/day only, assumed fall 2027 cycle). fees_usd from 2026-27 cost of attendance ($700). Health insurance not found (null). Majors are department/program names from the departments-and-programs page. | Sources: https://www.bowdoin.edu/admissions/apply/deadlines-requirements/index.html ; https://www.bowdoin.edu/admissions/apply/dates-deadlines/index.html ; https://www.bowdoin.edu/admissions/costs-and-aid/index.html ; https://www.bowdoin.edu/academics/departments-and-programs/index.html', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?161004-Bowdoin-College', '2026-10-05'),
  ('216597', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Accounting','Finance','Marketing','Economics','Management Information Systems','Real Estate','Chemical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Computer Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Nursing']::text[], ARRAY['Chemical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Computer Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Management Information Systems']::text[], '2026-27', 67776, 17694, 1024, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1395, 1510, 'optional', '{"EA": "2026-11-01", "ED": "2026-11-01", "ED2": "2027-01-15", "RD": "2027-01-15"}', 'CDS 2025-26 C12 avg HS GPA 3.87 but only 16% of first-years submitted GPA. English proof required (TOEFL/IELTS/Duolingo/PTE/Cambridge) with no minimum scores on current first-year page; older 2021-22 catalog value not used. Test-optional through 2026-27 cycle (Class of 2031). Deadlines Nov 1 (EA/EDI) and Jan 15 (EDII/RD) from dates-and-deadlines page, no year stated (next cycle assumed); first-year page elsewhere mentions Nov 10 / Jan 31 as test-score or plan-change dates. fees_usd = Undergraduate Student Services Fee 1,024 (CDS G1 2026-27; excludes $300 first-year orientation fee). Health insurance $3,165 is the 2026-27 annual plan cost quoted for international students on Villanova health-services page (page context may refer to graduate students; undergraduates and internationals are required to be insured). Majors partly from search excerpt of business/engineering/nursing pages. | some low-confidence values omitted | Sources: https://www.villanova.edu/content/dam/villanova/provost/decision_support/CDS-2025-2026-v3.pdf ; https://www.villanova.edu/university/undergraduate-admission/applying-to-villanova/first-year-applicants.html ; https://www.villanova.edu/university/undergraduate-admission/applying-to-villanova/dates-and-deadlines.html ; https://www.villanova.edu/university/health-services/health-center/student-insurance-requirements.html ; https://www.villanova.edu/university/business/academics/undergraduate-programs/degrees.html', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?216597-Villanova-University', '2026-10-05'),
  ('232946', 'community_college', ARRAY['Computer Science','Engineering','Information Technology','Business Administration','Biology','Science','Mathematics','Psychology','Cybersecurity','Nursing','Accounting','Liberal Arts']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Engineering','Information Technology','Biology','Science','Mathematics','Cybersecurity']::text[], '2026-27', 12409, 12684, 1080, NULL, 6.5, 76, 110, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"Spring": "2026-10-15", "Fall": "2027-05-01"}', 'Scores are placement thresholds for direct entry to the Associate Degree F-1 program: TOEFL iBT 76-91 / IELTS 6.5 / DET 110-120 enroll in ENG 111 + ESL 67; 92+ / 7+ / 125+ go straight to ENG 111; lower scores go to ESL Pathway or Intensive English. F-1 applications from outside the US: Fall window Feb 1-May 1, Spring Aug 1-Oct 15 (page gives no year; next occurrences shown). No minimum GPA stated; no SAT/ACT admission policy (SAT/ACT only for English placement); community colleges publish no CDS, so avg_gpa4 null. fees_usd computed: out-of-state per-credit Capital Fee $28.50 + Student Activities $4.00 + Auxiliary $3.50 = $36 x 30 credits; excludes NOVA All Access textbook fee $22.50/credit (opt-out). Out-of-state tuition is $421.90/credit. Health insurance cost not found. | Sources: https://www.nvcc.edu/admissions/apply/international/index.html ; https://www.nvcc.edu/admissions/tuition/index.html ; https://catalog.nvcc.edu/programs-degree-type/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?232946-Northern-Virginia-Community-College', '2026-10-05'),
  ('163426', 'community_college', ARRAY['Computer Science','Cybersecurity','Data Science','Engineering','Business Analytics','Accounting','Psychology','Nursing']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Cybersecurity','Data Science','Engineering']::text[], '2026-27', 14250, 16530, 2337.6, NULL, 6.5, 90, 110, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"Fall": "2027-06-01"}', 'Community college, open admission: no minimum GPA, no SAT/ACT stated; no CDS. English scores (DET 110, IELTS 6.5, TOEFL iBT 90) are the scores that place a student directly into degree study; lower scores lead to MC ESL Guided Placement Test, so they are placement thresholds rather than admission cutoffs. Deadline: Fall I-20 deadline for overseas applicants June 1 (year not stated, assumed 2027); spring deadline Oct 1 has already passed; transfer I-20 dates (Aug 1 / Dec 1) not included. fees_usd computed from 2026-27 non-resident fee schedule per credit hour (consolidated $78.40 + facility $7 + technology $5 + transportation $7 = $97.40) x 24 credits (12 per semester, fall+spring) = $2,337.60. Health insurance is the College''s estimated average of $800 per year (students must buy their own). | health_insurance_usd=800 | Sources: https://www.montgomerycollege.edu/international-students/getting-started/english-proficiency-required-testing-and-placement.html ; https://www.montgomerycollege.edu/international-students/index.html ; https://www.montgomerycollege.edu/_documents/paying-for-college/tuition/2026-2027-tuition-fee-schedule.pdf ; https://www.montgomerycollege.edu/international-students/getting-started/evidence-of-financial-support.html ; https://www.montgomerycollege.edu/academics/programs/index.html', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?163426-Montgomery-College', '2026-10-05'),
  ('131496', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Biology','Chemistry','Mathematics','Physics','Economics','Government','International Politics','Accounting','Finance','Nursing','Global Health']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Biology','Chemistry','Mathematics','Physics','Global Health']::text[], '2026-27', 68017, 20596, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1390, 1550, 'required', '{"EA": "2026-11-01", "RD": "2027-01-01"}', 'English test is recommended but not required, no minimum scores stated (all min_* null). No minimum GPA stated. CDS 2025-26 is hosted on a Box link that could not be read, so avg_gpa4 null. Deadlines Nov 1 EA / Jan 1 RD (month/day only; next cycle assumed). SAT/ACT required per page. fees_usd = student activities fee $105.50 per semester x 2 = 211 (amount taken from search excerpt of the Student Accounts page; page fetch did not display the number). Health insurance $4,450/yr (waivable). Majors from official academic-offerings page. | health_insurance_usd=4450 | some low-confidence values omitted | Sources: https://uadmissions.georgetown.edu/apply/international-applicants/ ; https://studentaccounts.georgetown.edu/tuition/undergraduate/ ; https://uadmissions.georgetown.edu/academic-offerings/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?131496-Georgetown-University', '2026-10-05'),
  ('235343', 'community_college', ARRAY['Business','Pre-Nursing','Computer Science','Aviation','Engineering','Information Technology','Fine Arts & Design','Pre-Health','Psychology','Communications']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Engineering','Information Technology','Pre-Health']::text[], '2026-27', 5263, 17310, 717, NULL, 5.5, 61, 95, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"Winter": "2026-12-09", "Spring": "2027-03-17", "Summer": "2027-06-16", "Fall": "2027-09-01"}', 'Community college (University Transfer program). No CDS; no average or minimum GPA stated; no SAT/ACT admission policy stated (SAT/ACT appear only as alternative English proof). IELTS 5.5 with no band below 5.0; DET 95 with no section below 90; TOEFL iBT 61. Deadlines are International Programs new-student deadlines per term (8:00 AM Pacific; transfer-in students one week later). fees_usd = fees for the 9-month academic year Fall 2026-Summer 2027 (tuition 12,330 not included). health_insurance_usd = 402 per term x 3 terms (computed from the per-term figure). | health_insurance_usd=1206 | Sources: https://www.greenriver.edu/international/admissions/english-requirements.html ; https://www.greenriver.edu/international/dates-deadlines.html ; https://www.greenriver.edu/international/costs-payments.html ; https://www.greenriver.edu/international/programs/university-transfer/index.html', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?235343-Green-River-College', '2026-10-05'),
  ('234669', 'community_college', ARRAY['Arts and Science (Transfer Associate)','Business (Transfer Associate)','Engineering: Chemical and Bio (Transfer Associate)','Engineering: Civil and Mechanical (Transfer Associate)','Engineering: Electrical and Computer (Transfer Associate)','Biology, Chemistry, Environmental & Earth Science (Transfer Associate)','Physics, Atmospheric Sciences, General Engineering (Transfer Associate)','Computer Science (BS)','Accounting (AAS)','Math Education (Transfer Associate)','Music (Transfer Associate)']::text[], ARRAY['Engineering: Chemical and Bio (Transfer Associate)','Engineering: Civil and Mechanical (Transfer Associate)','Engineering: Electrical and Computer (Transfer Associate)','Biology, Chemistry, Environmental & Earth Science (Transfer Associate)','Physics, Atmospheric Sciences, General Engineering (Transfer Associate)','Computer Science (BS)','Math Education (Transfer Associate)']::text[], '2026-27', 10502, 17310, 298, NULL, 6, 61, 95, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"Winter": "2026-11-23", "Spring": "2027-02-22", "Summer": "2027-05-25"}', 'Community college (open-door associate/transfer programs); no minimum GPA, no SAT policy and no Common Data Set average GPA found. TOEFL 61 iBT (500 PBT), IELTS 6.0 overall with all subscores 5.5+, Duolingo 95 with Production 75+; the college still defaults to the 0-120 TOEFL scale (new 1-6 equivalence pending). Deadlines are for students outside the US (Winter 2027, Spring 2027, Summer 2027); Fall 2027 not yet posted. fees_usd = mandatory fees per year (9 months) for Associate programs; health = medical insurance per year. Pages were read through the site WordPress REST API because the HTML pages returned 403 to my fetch. | health_insurance_usd=1377 | Sources: https://www.bellevuecollege.edu/international/future-students/english-scores/ ; https://www.bellevuecollege.edu/international/future-students/important-dates-deadlines/ ; https://www.bellevuecollege.edu/international/future-students/tuition/ ; https://www.bellevuecollege.edu/international/programs/college-level/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?234669-Bellevue-College', '2026-10-05'),
  ('116439', 'community_college', ARRAY['Computer Science','Engineering','Biological Sciences','Chemistry','Physics','Mathematics','Business Administration and Management','Accounting','Economics','Psychology','Film and Digital Media','Public Health Science']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Engineering','Biological Sciences','Chemistry','Physics','Mathematics']::text[], '2026-27', 11860, 25769, 52, NULL, 4.5, 52, 80, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"Spring": "2026-12-01", "Summer": "2027-04-10", "Fall": "2027-07-01"}', 'Community college (open admission, no CDS, no GPA or SAT requirement published). TOEFL iBT 52 for exams before 1/21/2026 (3.5 on new scale after); IELTS 4.5; Duolingo 80. Deadline pages give filing windows by month/day only (Spring Sep 1-Dec 1, Summer Feb 1-Apr 10, Fall Feb 1-Jul 1); closing dates used, next cycle assumed. fees_usd = only itemised mandatory fee, Health Center Fee $52/yr (2026-27 estimate; tuition $496/unit billed separately). Health insurance $2,580 annual plan (Aug 1 2026-Jul 31 2027); the expense estimate sheet budgets $2,400. | health_insurance_usd=2580 | Sources: https://www.ivc.edu/international/admission ; https://www.ivc.edu/international/application-deadlines ; https://www.ivc.edu/international/expenses ; https://www.ivc.edu/international/health-insurance ; https://www.ivc.edu/academics/programs', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?116439-Irvine-Valley-College', '2026-10-05'),
  ('113634', 'community_college', ARRAY['Computer Science','Civil Engineering','Electrical and Computer Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Biology','Environmental Science','Business Administration','Allied Health','Chemistry','Mathematics','Economics','Nutrition']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Civil Engineering','Electrical and Computer Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Biology','Environmental Science','Chemistry','Mathematics']::text[], '2026-27', 10320, 23238, 10, NULL, 5.5, 61, 95, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"Fall": "2027-07-01", "Spring": "2026-12-01"}', 'Community college; international applicant to associate/transfer programs. English: TOEFL iBT 61 (or 3.5 on new 1-6 scale), IELTS Academic 5.5 (minimum band 4.5), DET 95; lower scores (TOEFL 57, DET 90) accepted only for gap-year students or the Academic Bridge Program. No minimum GPA stated and no SAT/ACT required (sat_policy left null). Deadlines (applicants abroad): Fall July 1, Spring December 1 (Aug 1 and Jan 1 for applicants already in the US); pages give no year, so years inferred as the next terms. Costs 2026-27: international tuition $447/unit ($46 enrollment + $401 nonresident), 24 units = $10,728; fees_usd = mandatory Student Union Fee $1/unit capped at $10/year (Pleasant Hill courses); other fees are voluntary or course-specific. Mandatory health insurance $1,945/yr (Aug-Dec $810.15 + Jan-Jul $1,134.21; the intl.4cd.edu page shows an older $1,889). Total estimated cost for I-20 is $30,495. Majors taken from DVC program lists via official-domain search text. Avg GPA not applicable (open-admission, no CDS GPA). | health_insurance_usd=1945 | Sources: https://www.intl.4cd.edu/images/downloads/Evidence-of-English-Language-Proficiency.pdf ; https://www.intl.4cd.edu/admissions ; https://www.dvc.edu/financial-aid/tuition-fees ; https://www.dvc.edu/student-services/international-student-services/international-student-fees-payment-instructions ; https://www.dvc.edu/academics/explore-our-programs', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?113634-Diablo-Valley-College', '2026-10-05'),
  ('121044', 'community_college', ARRAY['Computer Science','Business Administration','Biology','Mathematics','Physics','Economics','Psychology','Geology','Environmental Science','Public Health','Kinesiology','Nutrition and Dietetics']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Biology','Mathematics','Physics','Geology','Environmental Science']::text[], '2026-27', 9820, 19431, 80, NULL, 5, 45, 80, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"Spring": "2026-11-30", "Fall": "2027-07-15"}', 'Community college (open admission): no CDS/GPA published, no stated minimum GPA, no SAT policy found. English minimums (any one): IELTS 5.0, TOEFL iBT 45, Duolingo 80, plus others; exemptions exist. Deadlines for students outside the US: Spring 2027 Nov 30 2026, Fall 2027 Jul 15 2027 (F-1 transfer Jan 15 / Jul 25). Fees: international budget lists tuition+fees $11,624 = $481/unit x 24 units + $80 student fees; fees_usd=80 is the student-fees part. Mandatory international health insurance $1,500 (estimate). Applies to Fall 2026-Summer 2027 entry. Majors from PCC transfer degree/pathway list. | health_insurance_usd=1500 | Sources: https://pasadena.edu/academics/international-students/apply/english-proficiency-requirements.php ; https://pasadena.edu/academics/international-students/apply/index.php ; https://pasadena.edu/academics/international-students/apply/tuition-and-fees.php ; https://pasadena.edu/academics/degrees-and-certificates/index.php', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?121044-Pasadena-City-College', '2026-10-05'),
  ('236939', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Electrical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Bioengineering','Mechanical Engineering','Accounting','Finance','Psychology','Biology','Kinesiology','Animal Sciences','Data Analytics']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Electrical Engineering','Civil Engineering','Bioengineering','Mechanical Engineering','Biology','Data Analytics']::text[], NULL, 29950, 13622, NULL, 2.7, 6.5, NULL, 105, 3.46, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"Spring": "2026-11-15", "Summer": "2027-03-15", "Fall": "2027-06-15"}', 'avg_gpa4 = CDS 2025-26 C12 (3.46). Min GPA 2.70 for international first-year (Traditional Admission). TOEFL iBT shown only on new 1-6 scale (4) so min_toefl null. SAT/ACT policy not stated on the international pages (SAT/ACT only listed as English-proficiency alternative) so null. Deadlines are month/day only; assumed next cycle (Spring 2027, Summer 2027, Fall 2027). fees_usd = computed 2 x $830/semester Pullman undergraduate mandatory fees (Rec Center, CUB, Stadium, Health, Technology, Transit, Chinook, Media, Food Pantry; S&A $636/sem is included in tuition); that page does not label the year, and CDS G1 text layout is scrambled (appears to show required fees $2,298), so fees uncertain; academic_year left null. health_insurance_usd $4,290/yr is the ISHIP estimate on the international tuition page (year not labeled, appears 2026-27). Majors from Registrar list as seen in search excerpt (PDF not fully read). | health_insurance_usd=4290 | some low-confidence values omitted | Sources: https://wpcdn.web.wsu.edu/wp-provost/uploads/sites/3285/2026/05/CDS_2025-2026-PDF_For-Website.pdf ; https://ip.wsu.edu/future-students/requirements/ ; https://ip.wsu.edu/future-students/deadlines-dates/ ; https://financialaid.wsu.edu/tuition-and-expenses/ ; https://ip.wsu.edu/future-students/tuition-fees/ ; https://registrar.wsu.edu/media/b54knjfs/undergraduate-majors-minors-and-certificates.pdf', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?236939-Washington-State-University', '2026-10-05'),
  ('236513', 'community_college', ARRAY['Computer Science','Engineering','Biology','Chemistry','Physics and Astronomy','Math','Business','Economics','Psychology','Earth Sciences','Environmental','Nutrition Science']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Engineering','Biology','Chemistry','Physics and Astronomy','Math','Earth Sciences','Environmental','Nutrition Science']::text[], '2026-27', 5745, 19041, 750, NULL, 6, 64, 100, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"Winter": "2026-11-25", "Spring": "2027-02-25", "Summer": "2027-05-25", "Fall": "2027-08-25"}', 'Community college (no Common Data Set), so avg_gpa4 null. English scores are the minimums for direct college-level placement (College Bridge Level 5 / full-time college): TOEFL iBT 64 with Writing 17 (old format; new scale 4.0 with Writing 4.0), IELTS Academic 6.0 with Writing 5.0, Duolingo 100 with Production 100; lower scores place into Intensive English / College Bridge levels (e.g. TOEFL 56, IELTS 5.5, Duolingo 90 for Bridge 3). No minimum GPA or SAT policy stated for international applicants (a GPA of 3.0 or top 20% applies only to English-medium school proof / under-18 applicants per site footnotes). Deadlines are for general applicants; transfer/concurrent/remote deadlines are about a month later. Fall 2026 general deadline was 2026-08-25 (passed). Cost page is Fall 2026 - Summer 2027 estimate for 9-month academic year: approximate fees $750, mandatory medical insurance $1,500, tuition $11,700 (15 credits/quarter). | health_insurance_usd=1500 | Sources: https://intl.seattlecolleges.edu/english-proficiency ; https://intl.seattlecolleges.edu/dates-and-deadlines ; https://intl.seattlecolleges.edu/cost ; https://seattlecentral.edu/programs/college-transfer/program-pathways', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?236513-Seattle-Central-College', '2026-10-05'),
  ('161086', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Biology','Economics','Government','Psychology','Mathematics','Statistics','Environmental Studies','Physics','Chemistry','Global Studies','Art History']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Biology','Mathematics','Statistics','Physics','Chemistry']::text[], '2026-27', 69600, 17890, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1460, 1550, 'optional', '{"ED": "2026-11-15", "ED2": "2027-01-04", "RD": "2027-01-04"}', 'English test (TOEFL/IELTS/DET) required if English is not first/current language, but NO minimum score published, so min_* null. avg_gpa4 null: no recent Colby CDS found. Deadlines page gives month/day only; assumed 2026-27 cycle. fees_usd = General Fee $3,200/yr and health_insurance_usd = $2,628 Anthem annual premium: FROM SEARCH EXCERPT of colby.edu Student Charges page (page itself is behind Cloudflare, not fetchable); first-years also pay $500 COOT fee (afa.colby.edu cost page). Majors from search excerpt of official majors page. | some low-confidence values omitted | Sources: https://afa.colby.edu/apply/requirements/ ; https://afa.colby.edu/apply/dates-and-deadlines/ ; https://wwwvip.colby.edu/academics/majors-minors/ ; https://www.colby.edu/people/offices-directory/student-financial-services/student-account-information/student-charges-payment-schedule/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?161086-Colby-College', '2026-10-05'),
  ('110334', 'community_college', ARRAY['Computer Science','Biology','Business','Accounting/Finance','Chemistry','Economics','Engineering','Mathematics','Nursing','Physics','Psychology','Computer and Information Systems']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Biology','Chemistry','Engineering','Mathematics','Physics','Computer and Information Systems']::text[], '2026-27', 9862, 25281, 218, NULL, 5.5, 54, 85, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"Spring": "2026-12-01", "Fall": "2027-07-01"}', 'Community college, open admission: no CDS found, no GPA or SAT/ACT requirement stated for international applicants. English minimums for admission: TOEFL iBT 54 (480 paper), IELTS Academic 5.5, Duolingo 85. Deadlines: Fall July 1 (suggested May 1), Spring Dec 1 (suggested Nov 1) - month/day only, assumed Fall 2027 and Spring 2027 cycles. fees_usd computed per year for 12 units, 2 semesters: health fee $28 + student activity card $10 + student center fee $5 (cap) + student representation $2 + transportation $40 + nonresident/international capital outlay fee $2/unit x 12 = $24 -> $109/semester = $218; excludes tuition, optional parking, course materials fees. International page budget (older estimate): tuition and fees $10,918, books and insurance $2,082 for two semesters; no separate insurance premium published (students buy own plan with at least $300,000 coverage), so health_insurance_usd null. Majors are the academic departments listed on the Cabrillo Academics and Careers page (catalog program list is a JavaScript app and could not be read). | Sources: https://www.cabrillo.edu/international/international-admission-requirements/ ; https://www.cabrillo.edu/admissions-and-records/fees-payments-and-refunds/ ; https://www.cabrillo.edu/academics-and-careers/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?110334-Cabrillo-College', '2026-10-05'),
  ('122977', 'community_college', ARRAY['Computer Science','Engineering','Business','Computer Information Systems','Accounting','Architecture','Graphic Design','Film Production','Journalism - Multimedia Storytelling','Nursing - RN','Early Childhood Education','Game Design Foundation']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Engineering','Computer Information Systems']::text[], '2026-27', 10708, 25908, 125, NULL, 5, 45, 75, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Community college (open admission): no HS GPA or SAT policy found (avg_gpa4, min_gpa4, sat_policy null). English minimums from ''SMC Proof of English Proficiency for F-1 Visa Applicants'' revised 10/09/25: TOEFL iBT 45 (old scale), IELTS 5.0, Duolingo 75. Deadlines are the out-of-country F-1 deadlines posted for Winter/Spring/Summer/Fall 2026 terms (Winter 2026 deadline is Nov 15, 2025); the page lists only 2026 terms so 2027 dates unknown. Costs for Fall 2026-Summer 2027: tuition+enrollment fee $486/unit (24 units = $11,664, not in fees_usd). fees_usd = health fee $28 + Associated Students $10 + Student Benefits $22.50 + Student Representation $2 per semester x2 = $125. Mandatory insurance $1,082 fall + $1,228 spring = $2,310 (plus $196 one-time initial fee in first semester). | health_insurance_usd=2310 | Sources: https://www.smc.edu/admission-aid/apply/international-students/documents/smc--iec-english-proficiency-10-9-25.pdf ; https://www.smc.edu/admission-aid/apply/international-students/ ; https://www.smc.edu/admission-aid/apply/international-students/tuition-fees.php ; https://www.smc.edu/student-support/academic-support/transfer-center/areas-of-study/associate-degrees/associate-degrees/as-degrees.php', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?122977-Santa-Monica-College', '2026-10-05'),
  ('235103', 'community_college', ARRAY['Business','Computer Science','Biology','Engineering','Psychology','Economics','Communication Studies','Pre-Nursing','Mathematics','Chemistry','Environmental Science','Music']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Biology','Engineering','Mathematics','Chemistry','Environmental Science']::text[], '2026-27', 10875, 17889, 754.65, NULL, 5, 54, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"Winter": "2026-12-07", "Spring": "2027-03-08"}', 'Community college (associate/transfer). Min scores from Edmonds ''English proficiency tests accepted'' sheet: TOEFL iBT 54, IELTS 5.0 overall (5.0 each band); applicants without a score may take the free Edmonds placement test. Duolingo only appears in a placement table (95+ for ENGL 101, 75 lowest), no admission minimum, so null. Deadlines are ''Overseas'' application deadlines per quarter (Winter 2027 Dec 7, Spring 2027 Mar 8). fees_usd = associated student fees $251.55/quarter (est. 15 credits) x 3 quarters (computed; other fees may apply). health_insurance_usd = mandatory plan $411.03/quarter x 3. No GPA or SAT policy (open admission, min age 16 or HS graduate). Majors from search excerpt of official transfer-degree pages. | health_insurance_usd=1233.09 | Sources: https://www.edmonds.edu/international/documents/engl-prof-edmondscc.pdf ; https://www.edmonds.edu/international/dates.html ; https://www.edmonds.edu/international/costs.html ; https://www.edmonds.edu/International/programs/university-transfer-programs.html', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?235103-Edmonds-College', '2026-10-05'),
