  ('235431', 'community_college', ARRAY['Business','Computer Science','Economics','Education','Hospitality and Tourism Management','Nursing','Pre-Medicine','Cybersecurity and Forensics','Respiratory Care','Applied Management','Youth Development','Integrated Design']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Cybersecurity and Forensics','Respiratory Care']::text[], '2026-27', 5332, 15228, NULL, NULL, 5.5, 54, 90, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"Winter": "2026-11-25", "Spring": "2027-02-26"}', 'Community college (open admission; no CDS, GPA minimum or SAT policy published). IELTS 5.5 with no band below 5.0; TOEFL iBT 54; Duolingo 90. Deadlines are ''preferred'' deadlines for applicants outside the US (Winter 2027 Nov 25 2026, Spring 2027 Feb 26 2027); Summer/Fall 2027 not yet posted. Fees: tuition and fees are published combined only (2025-26 estimate $13,000/yr incl. fees), plus $120 one-time ISP orientation fee -> fees_usd null. Health insurance = $447.84/quarter effective Fall 2026 x 3 quarters = $1,343.52 (computed; charged with tuition). | health_insurance_usd=1343.52 | Sources: https://international.highline.edu/future-students/english-proficiency/ ; https://international.highline.edu/future-students/dates/ ; https://international.highline.edu/current-students/insurance/ ; https://international.highline.edu/programs/degrees-majors/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?235431-Highline-College', '2026-10-05'),
  ('119164', 'community_college', ARRAY['Accounting','Business/Economics','Computer Science','Computer Information Systems','Big Data Analytics','Engineering','Biology','Chemistry','Mathematics','Physics','Environmental Studies','Nutrition']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Computer Information Systems','Big Data Analytics','Engineering','Biology','Chemistry','Mathematics','Physics','Environmental Studies']::text[], '2026-27', 10464, 25587, 98, NULL, 4.5, NULL, 75, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"Spring": "2026-11-15", "Summer": "2027-04-30"}', 'Community college (open admission, no GPA/SAT policy). TOEFL iBT minimum shown only on new scale (3.5) so min_toefl null; IELTS 4.5, Duolingo 75. Deadlines F-1 new: Spring Nov 15 2026, Summer intersession Apr 30 2027 (Fall 2027 deadline not yet posted). fees_usd $98 = health $46 + student activities $30 + representation $4 + transportation $18 per year; excludes per-unit enrollment fee ($46 x 24 units = $1,104), nonresident tuition and insurance. health_insurance_usd = computed 2 x $762.18 mandatory LewerMark plan. Majors from Guided Pathways STEM/business pages. | health_insurance_usd=1524.36 | Sources: https://www.mtsac.edu/international/application_process.html ; https://www.mtsac.edu/international/tuition_fees.html ; https://www.mtsac.edu/international/student_health_insurance.html ; https://www.mtsac.edu/guided-pathways/science-programs.html', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?119164-Mt-San-Antonio-College', '2026-10-05'),
  ('110422', 'undergraduate', ARRAY['Computer Science','Software Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Computer Engineering','Aerospace Engineering','Civil Engineering','Industrial Engineering','Biomedical Engineering','Architecture','Business Administration','Economics']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Software Engineering','Mechanical Engineering','Electrical Engineering','Computer Engineering','Aerospace Engineering','Civil Engineering','Industrial Engineering','Biomedical Engineering']::text[], NULL, 34665, 18792, NULL, NULL, 6.5, 80, 115, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"Fall": "2026-11-30", "FileCompletion": "2027-02-15"}', 'avg_gpa4 null: CDS 2025-26 C12 reports 4.03 (weighted GPA, above 4.0 scale); Cal Poly uses 9th-11th grade weighted GPA. TOEFL 80 for exams before 2026-01-21 (new scale 4.5). English waiver possible after 3 years of English-medium instruction. Filing period Oct 1 - Nov 30 via Cal State Apply, file completion Feb 15 (page gives no year; inferred 2026-27 cycle). SAT/ACT policy not confirmed on an official page (CDS checkbox unreadable) -> null. Fees: Cal Poly publishes combined tuition and fees only, mandatory fees not separable -> null; health insurance not found -> null. Majors from admissions.calpoly.edu list. | Sources: https://www.calpoly.edu/admissions/international-student/selection-criteria/english-exam-requirements ; https://www.calpoly.edu/admissions/international-student/dates-and-deadlines ; https://admissions.calpoly.edu/majors', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?110422-California-Polytechnic-State-University-San-Luis-Obispo', '2026-10-05'),
  ('247834', 'community_college', ARRAY['General Studies (AA)','General Studies (AS)','Business Field of Study (AA)','Criminal Justice (AA)','Political Science (AA)','Psychology (AA)','Sociology (AA)','Communication (AA)','Biology (AS)','Associate of Arts in Teaching']::text[], ARRAY['Biology (AS)']::text[], '2025-26', 6064, 9379, NULL, NULL, 6.5, 71, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"Fall": "2027-06-01"}', 'Community college; new F-1 degree-seeking applicants. TOEFL iBT 71 for tests before Jan 21 2026 (new-scale entry on the page was garbled; search excerpt says 4). Duolingo not accepted per search excerpt. Deadlines: Fall June 1 (assumed Fall 2027); Spring Oct 1 2026 already passed. fees_usd is COMPUTED, not published: $2/credit-hour student activity fee (2025-26 schedule: 3 hrs = $606 vs $200 per hr) x 12 credits x 2 terms = $48, plus $2 per-term student record fee x 2 = $4, total $52; assumes full-time F-1 load of 12 hours in Fall and Spring. No CDS used (community college). Majors from search excerpt of program pages. Health insurance not found. Page requires $33,500 funds documentation. | some low-confidence values omitted | Sources: https://www.collin.edu/advising/international/initial_F-1_Applicants ; https://www.collin.edu/student-financial-services/documents/2025-26-tuition-schedule.pdf ; https://www.collin.edu/academics/programs/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?247834-Collin-County-Community-College-District', '2026-10-05'),
