  ('122889', 'community_college', ARRAY['Computer Science','Engineering','Biology','Business Administration','Chemistry','Economics','Mathematics','Nursing (ADN)','Physics','Psychology','Communication Studies','Art History']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Engineering','Biology','Chemistry','Mathematics','Physics']::text[], '2026-27', 10432, 22086, 140, 2, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"Spring": "2026-11-15", "Summer": "2027-04-01", "Fall": "2027-06-01"}', 'Community college: min GPA = equivalent of 2.00 US GPA (transcripts requirement). TOEFL/IELTS not required for academic programs (English proficiency can be shown several ways), so test minimums null. No SAT/ACT policy stated. Deadlines for new students (transfer/current F-1 students have later dates): Spring Nov 15, Summer Apr 1, Fall Jun 1; month/day only, assumed next upcoming cycle (Spring 2027, Summer 2027, Fall 2027). fees_usd computed for Fall 2026 + Spring 2027 (24 units): Student Activity Pass $16 + Mandatory Health Fee $56 + Transportation Fee $64 + Student Representation Fee $4 = $140; tuition/enrollment fees ($10,776) excluded. Mandatory medical insurance $1,890 for the two semesters. | health_insurance_usd=1890 | Sources: https://www.sbcc.edu/international/prospective/steps-to-apply-full-time-student.php ; https://www.sbcc.edu/international/prospective/current-fees.php ; https://catalog.sbcc.edu/programs/a-z/', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?122889-Santa-Barbara-City-College', '2026-10-05'),
  ('225423', 'community_college', ARRAY['Computer Science','Engineering Science','Biology','Chemistry','Physics','Mathematics','Business','Computer Information Systems','Artificial Intelligence','Psychology','Nursing','Geology']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Science','Engineering Science','Biology','Chemistry','Physics','Mathematics','Computer Information Systems','Artificial Intelligence','Geology']::text[], '2026-27', 5460, 9330, 1836, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"Spring": "2026-10-15", "Summer": "2027-03-15"}', 'HCC says TOEFL is not required for admission; academic-program students must show English proficiency via TOEFL, IELTS, PTE, TOEIC, ACCUPLACER ESL or an approved TSI test with no published minimum scores, so min_* null. Deadlines are F-1 outside-US dates (Fall Jun 15, Spring Oct 15, Summer Mar 15); page gives month/day only; years assumed (Fall 2026 date already passed). fees_usd computed from 2026-27 out-of-state fee components: General Fee $50/hr + Technology $25/hr x 24 hours, Student Activity $1/hr (max $12/semester) x 2, Recreation $6/semester x 2 = $1,836 (tuition $151/hr excluded; page total $227/hr). health_insurance_usd = BCBS plan via Academic HealthPlans, Fall $1,037 + Spring/Summer $1,537 (2026-27), automatic for F-1 students; source is the plan administrator PDF linked from hccs.edu. No minimum GPA stated; no CDS so avg_gpa4 null. | health_insurance_usd=2574 | Sources: https://www.hccs.edu/admissions/apply--enroll/international-student-application/first-time-f-1-student/ ; https://www.hccs.edu/paying-for-college/tuition--cost/the-financial-aid-cost-of-attendance/ ; https://myahpcare.com/wp-content/uploads/HCC_PC-26-27.pdf ; https://www.hccs.edu/programs--courses/explore-all-programs/?track=University+Transfer', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?225423-Houston-City-College', '2026-10-05'),
  ('227182', 'community_college', ARRAY['Accounting AAS','Business Administration AAS','Computer Programming Specialist AAS','Cybersecurity AAS','Game Design and Simulation AAS','Geographic Information Systems AAS','Mechanical Design Technology AAS','Industrial Electronics Technology AAS','Instrumentation Technology AAS','Process Technology AAS','Professional Pilot AAS','Logistics Management AAS']::text[], ARRAY['Computer Programming Specialist AAS','Cybersecurity AAS','Game Design and Simulation AAS','Geographic Information Systems AAS','Mechanical Design Technology AAS','Industrial Electronics Technology AAS','Instrumentation Technology AAS','Process Technology AAS']::text[], '2025-26', 9390, 10756, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 50, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '{"Spring": "2026-11-01", "Fall": "2027-07-01"}', 'Community college (open admission): no GPA, no SAT policy. English minimums are exactly as published (composite minimums for admission: TOEFL iBT 19, IELTS 2, Duolingo 50 - very low, ESOL/developmental placement likely; scores for direct eligibility for the TSI test are TOEFL iBT 71, IELTS 6.0, Duolingo 100). Deadlines are month/day only for applicants outside the U.S. (Fall Jul 1, Spring Nov 1), assumed next cycle. fees_usd=0: LSC says tuition simplification folded fees into tuition (fee per credit hour $0.00 in tuition history table through 2025-26); international tuition 2026-27 is $313 per credit hour inclusive. health_insurance_usd = mandatory LSC student health insurance annual cost from 2025-26 F-1 cost estimate page. Majors are the AAS programs approved for F-1 students (transfer AA/AS list not retrieved). | health_insurance_usd=2220 | some low-confidence values omitted | Sources: https://www.lonestar.edu/english-proficiency-requirement.htm ; https://www.lonestar.edu/f1admissions.htm ; https://www.lonestar.edu/tuition.htm ; https://www.lonestar.edu/international-tuition.htm ; https://www.lonestar.edu/f1programs', 'https://collegescorecard.ed.gov/school/?227182-Lone-Star-College-System', '2026-10-05'),
